-- only as a choice. Written with tools/courtesy_lines_check.py, which holds the rules and writes
-- what stands between LINES BEGIN and LINES END; the tests hold the pack to them. Its lines are
-- also the suite's own (ns.CourtesyLines): the situations the editor and the player's lines know.
-- luacheck: ignore 631 (a line stays one line, so that it can be read and edited as one)
